{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 proof that for the simple random walk on ℤ², almost surely the maximal local time Tₙ up to time n satisfies 1/(4π) ≤ liminf Tₙ/(log n)² ≤ limsup Tₙ/(log n)² ≤ 1/π (Erdős and Taylor 1960). The development is elementary: block independence and the fixed-time Markov property, exact return counts by the 45° rotation and Wallis' product, renewal at the first return, last-exit decomposition, Borel–Cantelli along dyadic and geometric times.",
